==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Grand Lucifer''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Almighty Lucifer''' at level 30 using [[Catfruit]] and XP.

==Strategy/Usage==
Lucifer the Fallen is an effective backline attacker with both excellent range to keep him outside the reach of most enemies and high DPS for said range, which is helped by a Surge and the Strong ability against two traits. His slow-ish attacks and large blindspot, combined with mediocre health, make him particularly weak against rushdown enemies, such as [[Bore]], but he works really well against most longer ranged enemies, such as [[Le'boin]] or [[Mooth]]. Since most armies tend to have a bit of both, it is always best to summon Lucifer the Fallen late in the fight, after a powerful frontline is established, so he may live long and attack safely.

Unlike most similar units, Lucifer the Fallen uses Surges to partly cover his blindspot, rather than to extend his reach, making him somewhat better in most situations, as the bulk of the enemies tends to be closer to the inner range than the furthest reach; in other words, the Surge acts as a balancing factor, improving on this unit's weakness instead of capitalising on his strength. It is worthy to mention, however, that his Surge helps to boost his DPS by a considerable amount: 3.5k to 5.3k at level 30. For his LD range of 450-750, his DPS is not something to ignore.

Of course, thanks to his Strong ability, Lucifer the Fallen shines the most against [[:Category:Floating Enemies|Floating]] and [[:Category:Aku Enemies|Aku]]. All throughout the game, Floating is a common trait, often given to strong bosses or long ranged common enemies, which is highly beneficial to this unit; just beware of [[Brollow]]s and [[Zollow]]s! Even against them, he is a fairly decent counter due to his surge walling them off when they spawn. Although he lacks a way to deal with Shields, his Surge is quite likely to hit whoever gets their shield destroyed by his main attack, mitigating the issue. Surge Immunity and the high damage per hit, on the other hand, help immensely, making Lucifer the Fallen overall effective against this trait.

==='''True Form'''===
Almighty Lucifer gains only two changes, that being a very small health increase and his guaranteed Surge attacks. Having more health is always good, especially since he has the Strong ability, but the more notable change is his guaranteed Surge generation chance. There is still the element of RNG in its spawn locations, but it significantly increases his chances of intercepting nasty peons and chipping durable enemies, improving his DPS by a large margin. For stats, his DPS is increased to 7k DPS at level 30, incredibly high for his range mark. This turns Lucifer into a very strong generalist as well as an incredibly effective specialist against Floating/Aku. The sheer power held by it, however, is slightly offset by it requiring an Epic Catfruit Seed (only obtainable after clearing [[Eldritch Forces]] from [[Growing Epic]] or randomly from Floor [[Infernal Tower/Floor 10|10]] and [[Infernal Tower/Floor 20|20]] of [[Infernal Tower]]).

==='''Talents'''===
For such a cheap price tag, '''Target Angel''' gives Almighty Lucifer an entirely new set of targets. In general, his range provides with him amazing matchups all across the board as a counter to the endless list of Angel frontline pushers like [[St. Dober]], [[Winged Pigge]], [[Boraphim]], etc, as well as midrangers/backliners like [[Cala Maria]] and [[Great Angel Chibinel]]. This Talent should be your main priority given how powerful of a trait this is for Lucifer to take advantage.

'''[[Survive|Survives]]''' is also a decent extension to his survivability, however, it is entirely unnecessary thanks to his high effective HP and good knockback count. Unlocking it isn't a bad idea per se, but it is very expensive for such a small layer of security.

'''[[Special Abilities#Resist|Resist Freeze]]''' is not particularly useful under most circumstances as Lucifer is usually content to completely outrange his targets, making this Talent counterintuitive. It sees niche applicability against [[Wicked Face]], but shouldn't be considered even then as he functions just fine without it.

Finally, since Almighty Lucifer is a stats-based unit, '''Attack Buff''' and '''HP Buff''' should be considered only after upgrading him with [[Catseye]]s.

